('P', 'DSM-5-TR criteria, paraphrased (APA, 2022); use the manual itself for formal diagnosis. A pervasive pattern, beginning by early adulthood, with **4 or more** of:'),
('B', 'Preoccupied with **details, rules, lists, order, or schedules** to the point that the main purpose of the activity is lost.'),
('B', '**Perfectionism that interferes with finishing tasks.**'),
('B', 'Excessively **devoted to work and productivity** at the expense of leisure and friendships (not explained by financial need).'),
