('B', '**Cluster C trial:** among 50 patients with avoidant, dependent, or obsessive-compulsive personality disorder, 40 sessions of cognitive or short-term dynamic therapy led to improvement maintained over 2 years; 42% (cognitive) and 54% (dynamic) recovered from symptoms, and about 40% in each group recovered in interpersonal problems and personality functioning (Svartberg et al., 2004).'),
('B', '**Schema therapy:** in a multicenter trial of 323 patients with Cluster C, paranoid, histrionic, or narcissistic personality disorder, schema therapy led to recovery more often than usual care or another psychotherapy (Bamelis et al., 2014).'),
